# flyrank

Early-stage Node.js project. Match existing patterns as the codebase grows.

## Code changes

- Keep diffs minimal — solve the requested problem only; avoid drive-by refactors.
- Read surrounding code before editing; reuse existing abstractions instead of duplicating logic.
- Prefer simple, direct implementations over premature abstraction.
- Add comments only for non-obvious business logic or tricky technical details.
- Add tests only when requested or when they cover meaningful behavior.

## Node / TypeScript

- Use ESM unless the repo already uses CommonJS.
- Prefer `async/await` over raw promise chains.
- Validate external input at boundaries (API routes, CLI args, env parsing).
- Never commit secrets — use `.env` locally; document required vars in README.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — silent failure
try {
  await fetchData();
} catch (e) {}

// ✅ GOOD — log and rethrow with context
try {
  await fetchData();
} catch (e) {
  console.error('Failed to fetch data', e);
  throw e;
}
```

## Git

- Do not create commits or push unless explicitly asked.
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or build artifacts (`dist/`, `node_modules/`).
